From: agx-linux-kit
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: do not index reference_frame_ts[] with -1

ref_frame_idx[] is -1 for a reference slot that a frame does not use (key
frames and intra-only frames). avd-av1.c used it to index
reference_frame_ts[8] without a range check, which UBSAN reports as
"index -1 is out of range for type '__u64 [8]'" and reads the 8 bytes before
the array.

Add avd_av1_ref_buf(): an unused or out of range slot gives the destination
buffer, the same result avd_get_ref_buf() already gives for an unknown
timestamp, so decode output does not change. set_ref_hdr() skips slot pairs
with an invalid index.

Tested: compiles without warnings with the M3 kernel build flags (7.2.11-m3gpu+).
Not tested on hardware: loading the module needs root.
---
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-av1.c	2026-10-28 02:25:43
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-av1.c	2026-10-28 02:26:40
@@ -330,6 +330,27 @@
 		 * (1 << WARP_PARAM_REDUCE_BITS);
 	*delta = AV1_DIV_ROUND_UP_POW2_SIGNED(*delta, WARP_PARAM_REDUCE_BITS)
 		* (1 << WARP_PARAM_REDUCE_BITS);
+}
+
+/*
+ * ref_frame_idx[] holds -1 for a slot the frame does not use (key frames,
+ * intra-only frames). Never index reference_frame_ts[] with it directly.
+ */
+static bool avd_av1_ref_idx_valid(int idx)
+{
+	return idx >= 0 && idx < V4L2_AV1_TOTAL_REFS_PER_FRAME;
+}
+
+/* Like avd_get_ref_buf(): an unused slot gives the destination buffer. */
+static struct avd_decoded_buffer *
+avd_av1_ref_buf(struct avd_ctx *ctx, struct avd_decoded_buffer *dst,
+		const struct v4l2_ctrl_av1_frame *frame, int idx)
+{
+	if (!avd_av1_ref_idx_valid(idx))
+		return dst;
+
+	return avd_get_ref_buf(ctx, &dst->base.vb,
+			       frame->reference_frame_ts[idx]);
 }
 
